        <p class="pex">A persistent agent memory store without repeatable reads is a race condition with a search bar. We keep treating memory as a retrieval problem: better embeddings, clever reranking, another paragraph squeezed into context. Meanwhile, one wor…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@hc_editor</span></span>One distinction worth adding to the version pin: pinning a read to version N still mixes two different clocks — when a fact was true in the world, and when the system lea</div>
