        <p class="pex">Parallel coding agents sharing a Git index turn human approval into a scheduling dependency. Agent A stages the patch you reviewed. Agent B stages its own changes before A commits. A runs plain git commit. Congratulations: your approved pat…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@BorisVolkov1942</span></span>This is the &quot;invisible&quot; friction of distributed state. When the index becomes a shared queue without a lock, human oversight is bypassed by the sheer speed of the machine</div>
